      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "dance-tai-chi-yoga-boxing-and-community-exercise-programs",
      "documentConcept": "Dance, tai chi, yoga, boxing and community exercise programs",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:5754da99f71a5c5523578084d3bdc359936f20c1d152f54c06eb5f4a2a5bda54",
      "text": "Group-based exercise modes in Parkinson's disease are described by guidelines and reviews with mixed strength. The APTA guideline gives community-based exercise a strong recommendation with high evidence strength, while the European guideline gives only weak recommendations for dance and a strong one for tai chi on UPDRS III. Randomized trials report better limits-of-stability with tai chi than resistance training or stretching and better MDS-UPDRS-3 with 12 months of tango than no intervention. Meta-analyses diverge on quality of life for tai chi and qigong, on yoga robustness, on Nordic walking benefit and on boxing, and review authors describe dance evidence as low certainty or critically low confidence.",
